{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/813286-2ed-lie-dissonance-and-quiescence","id":813286,"title":"[2ED] Lie, Dissonance and Quiescence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-21T04:52:40-08:00","id":813286,"title":"[2ED] Lie, Dissonance and Quiescence","content":"Topic for three core terms in <b>Mage</b> setting, that are also often confused. Discussion to hammer and showing concepts in 2ED universe of it. First, short sum up.<br /> <br /> <b>Lie</b> \u2013 collection of false facts about reality that Sleepers believe in. All of \u201cmagic does not exists\u201d, \u201cgod/goddess are not literal beings\u201d, \u201cthere is only this material world\u201d. Contrast to the Truth mages uncover in their lives after Awakening.<br /> <br /> <b>Dissonance</b> \u2013 effect of making magic more unstable by Abyssal Sympathy ( \u201cShard\u201d ) all Sleepers have in their souls. In 1ED known as Disbelieve, but do not connected to the convocation of Sleepers. Even Sleepers firmly believing in magic make Dissonance.<br /> <br /> <b>Quiescence</b> \u2013 also known as <i>Sleeping Curse</i>. Effect of Sleepers <b><i>instinctual</i></b> rejecting Supernal Magic, and forgetting about spell events. <i>Quiescence</i> is also harming Sleepers soul, lowering their <i>Integrity </i>trait ( i.e. making them a bit less emotional stable ).<br /> <br /> And I have probably the best definition of <i>Quiescence</i> and it\u2019s confrontation with general population <i>Integrity</i> in comic media. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Straight from <b>Dresden Files \u201cWelcome to the Jungle\u201d</b> story \u2013 just after Harry Dresden acknowledges that the he used magic to the Sleeper's face\u2026<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/bYmYjft.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/bYmYjft.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> Is it correct? If not, where I make mistake in understanding?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-22-2016, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T04:58:27-08:00","id":813288,"title":"","content":"Huh. That actually is rather spot-on, in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T08:22:50-08:00","id":813385,"title":"","content":"Basically. The Lie, the Masquerade, the Veil, G-M hiding? All the supernatural in the CofD tend to rely on a generalized &quot;Doubting Thomas&quot; effect. The general populous don't acknowledge the supernatural even if they live side by side with it. This effect is dialed up in Mage. Quintessence is actually a supernatural compulsion forcing people to ignore Awakened magic. Its still a Doubting Thomas effect, but its a DT effect enforced by Abyssal magic. In an ideal world, people wouldn't doubt they've seen anything supernatural. But, in the Fallen World, people are magically broken/castrated and blinded.<br /> <br /> Dissonance is when that doubting thomas effect triggers. It causes people to disbelieve they saw anything as well as rip into the magic they witnessed. <br /> <br /> I've seen The Lie used interchangably with describing the state of the Fallen World as well as another name for the Quintessence curse. I tend to think that the words are used interchangably - Lie as the common name, Quintessence as the formal/scientific name. Its like the difference between &quot;dog&quot; and &quot;canis lupis famiiaris.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T08:44:46-08:00","id":813398,"title":"","content":"While The Lie and The Masquerade serve the same purpose (which is to keep humanity guessing), I wouldn't attribute them the same narrative weight. One is virtually inescapable, the other can very well be subverted, even broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T10:13:52-08:00","id":813460,"title":"","content":"One thing I like about the design of Requiem and Awakening (and probably Forsaken, but I am not familiar with it) so far, especially for 2e, is that there are mechanical effects that enforce or hint at the creation of in-game cultural restrictions such as the Veil and Masquerade. It allows characters within the setting to have good reasons to enforce their secrecy, and at the same time if a member of that culture doesn't enforce it, the world itself will cover some of their tracks and impose some penalty. In this manner, even a newly Awakened or Embraced realizes by themselves that they need to hide, even without a mentor. Of course, without a mentor, the process is going to be painful and might get you killed or worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T11:38:14-08:00","id":813516,"title":"","content":"I agree with Wyrdhampster's interpretation, from what I've seen in the development blogs. I was never able to get into Mage in 1e, I was one of those people that got turned off by the core book and never dug enough into later material to learn how much more interesting the setting actually is than the core book made it look. So with that in mind, here is my understanding from what I've read about 2e.<br /> <br /> <b>The Lie</b> is the feeling of powerlessness that we all feel at some point in our lives. It's the notion that humanity is small and insignificant in the face of a vast and uncaring universe. It's the little voice in our heads that tells us to keep our heads down, fall in line, don't make waves, we're not special and we're not important. Depending on how Mage-centric your crossover swings, this may be the cause of that Doubting Thomas Effect that we see in other lines, or it may just be another expression of that same phenomenon. Either way, it is a large part of what keeps people from Awakening, and it has a strong connection to the Supernal symbols of oppression that the Awakened refer to as the Exarchs. The Atlantis myth casts them as Ascended Mages from the time before that wove themselves into the Supernal and created the symbols of the Lie to keep humanity under control and prevent them from Awakening and eventually Ascending.<br /> <br /> <b>Dissonance</b> is the result of the symbols of unreality (which the Awakened refer to as The Abyss) woven into the soul of every human being affected by The Lie (whom the Awakened refer to as Sleepers). When a Sleeper comes into contact with Supernal magic, the Abyssal symbols in her soul reacts with the Supernal symbols that the Mage uses to cast his spell in a manner similar to how anti-matter interacts with normal matter. The Sleeper's soul and the Mage's spell are both damaged by this conflict, and unreality may seep into reality in a phenomenon the Awakened call Paradox. For reasons that should be fairly obvious but suffer from &quot;why doesn't it work like it did in cWoD&quot; syndrome, this interaction occurs regardless of the Sleeper's awareness of or belief in magic. However, some humans are able to shed the shard of Abyss in their soul without actually Awakening, with one of the easiest ways to do this being <i>gaining magical or supernatural abilities</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Quiessence</b>, also known as the Sleeping Curse, is the soul's self-defense mechanism against the harm caused to it by Dissonance. the Sleeper subconsciously attempts to rationalize what they've experienced in a way that complies with The Lie. Failing that, they will outright suppress the memory. Again, depending on how Mage-centric your crossover swings, this may be the cause of other, similar memory-altering phenomena like Lunacy, or it may be unrelated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-21-2016, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T19:31:01-08:00","id":813845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/813286-2ed-lie-dissonance-and-quiescence?p=813398#post813398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While The Lie and The Masquerade serve the same purpose (which is to keep humanity guessing), I wouldn't attribute them the same narrative weight. One is virtually inescapable, the other can very well be subverted, even broken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, but Wyrdhamster pretty much nailed it regardless. Lunancy is closer but still doesn't have quite the double team effect of dissonance and quiescence then you add the wildcard of paradox.<br /> <br /> Quiensense is both an advantage and disadvantage. Unless you're a supernatural or a sleepwalker you absolutely will not find or have a chance against a mage. But it's a double edged sword because of dissonance and paradox.<br /> <br /> For a mage there rarely is a middle ground when dealing with sleepers and it's very risky when using magic against supernaturals because of Clash of Wills. Seems absolutely fitting for a game and supernatural type that is all about power, wisdom, corruption and the balance between the three.<br /> <br /> Luckily a mage rules supreme in information and intelligence gathering. Mage Sight when used at the focused level literally gives them all their targets actual capabilities down to the dot levels of their stats on the sheet for every mage and more if you're an Adamantine Arrow.<br /> <br /> Time and planning is a nasty thing ESPECIALLY if you have 2 dots in the Time Arcanum. If you find yourself in a scrap just keep rewinding time for that last round until you find the right choice.<br /> <br /> This is why a mage or myself doesn't give a damn about a Kindred or Uratha in most cases because only fire fights fire. Apostates are wildcards, Banishers are deadly and the Mad are rabid dogs. All use the sane mage's weapons and have the same abilities and most times the same strategies and tactics.<br /> <br /> Mages absolutely kick ass and take names but it's all about picking the best choice in every situation when there isn't actually any good choice ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 01-22-2016, 12:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T03:34:23-08:00","id":814023,"title":"","content":"For a vampire, the primary reason to keep the Maquerade is a social one. This is fitting for a social-political game. Mage is a game about exploration, Mysteries, learning, growing, and creating society. In other words, mental exploration. Naturally, mage is going to have their Must Hide equivalent rooted in those mental areas. The threat of the Lie is also higher for mages for a simple reason - Doubting Thomas is their weakness. Vampires have sunlight issues in this game in no small part because its a social challenge - daylight is when majority of humans do things. Mages struggle against fear and ignorance, the magical equivalents of science denial. <br /> <br /> In short, despite being Hide!! equivalents, they serve vastly different purposes in the narrative. Its much like Wisdom versus Humanity. Sure, they are both karma meters, but that is all they have in common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T03:51:02-08:00","id":814025,"title":"","content":"I don't think the example from Dresden Files is exactly right (or at least that section didn't get it across on it's own). It's not fear that drives the sleeping curse, it's a defence against being damaged.<br /> <br /> Interestingly though the Praetorians think that's the case. If you're a Seer it probably helps to see the sleeping curse as an inherent character flaw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T01:39:43-08:00","id":815310,"title":"","content":"I tend to downplay the Quiescence in my own games while amping up the Dissonance. This makes mages more like vampires, more genuinely afraid of mortals, and less flippant about casting in public. More Paradox, with harsher consequences, spells being disbelieved, it all adds up to the theme that what mages do is fundamentally unnatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T18:54:22-08:00","id":817318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/813286-2ed-lie-dissonance-and-quiescence?p=815310#post815310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to downplay the Quiescence in my own games while amping up the Dissonance. This makes mages more like vampires, more genuinely afraid of mortals, and less flippant about casting in public. More Paradox, with harsher consequences, spells being disbelieved, it all adds up to the theme that what mages do is fundamentally unnatural.</div> </div> </div> </div> I like that idea! Do you have any house rules, or is just a matter of emphasis?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T19:31:24-08:00","id":817336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/813286-2ed-lie-dissonance-and-quiescence?p=817318#post817318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I like that idea! Do you have any house rules, or is just a matter of emphasis?</div> </div> </div> </div>I do have some houserules for 2e (I've shied away from running or playing Mage, and only lately have come around to the idea of doing so). Right now, my tentative houserules is to start every single spell with baseline Paradox (so instead of a free Reach, you always risk Paradox no matter how casual the spell is). In 1e, I'd get rid of the Vulgar/Covert system and run all spells as automatically risking Paradox at all times. For Quiescence, I'd run it closer to Lunacy, with the idea that mortals with high Willpower (or that succeed at their Integrity roll) can actually remember what happened, and are likely to become Hunters. I might steal the 2e Lunacy rules and have dramatic failures in the Integrity roll bestow the Proximi minor template.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I also might tweak the Disbelief rules to make sure that mages can't feasibly cast anything that would have any long-term permanent consequences on humanity, like mind-controlling authority figures or any such shenanigans. I'll probably adjust Disbelief so that it can reasonably keep magic in check.<br /> <br /> In terms of fluff, my baseline assumption is that mages are completely deluded about the nature of reality. Everything in the Mage books is true, when observed by a Mage. For everyone else, the Supernal Realms are nightmarish hell planes of soul-murder, and the Abyss is the stalwart guardian of humanity against the incursions of the aforementioned planes. Since humanity has a sympathetic connection to the Abyss, I reasoned that the Abyss is probably <i>a very good thing for humanity</i>. I also have Abyssal entities consider regular humans to be kin, to drive this point home. Where Mages see their souls as having &quot;awakened into the truth&quot;, everyone else sees their souls as missing a vital component, which was replaced by a shard of the hellish realms. Paradox, then, is the Abyss trying to protect humanity from the Supernal soul-murder.<br /> <br /> Of course, Exarchs are still the bad guys (because they use the Supernal to actively oppress humanity) and Mad Ones are still terribly dangerous, but even Pentacle mages are hubristic and misguided. Banishers are the closest thing to &quot;heroic mages&quot;, from humanity's perspective, and Scelesti are... complicated.<br /> <br /> This viewpoint emphasises an aspect of hubris that I thought wasn't terribly well explored in either edition of mage (though I'd have to read 2e properly to say for sure): the idea that hubris <i>blinds</i>. That mages are convinced that their delusions about reality are true, and that their hubris blinds them to the idea that they might be wrong, that their actions may not, in fact, be justified. That maybe humanity, in its powerlessness and sympathy for the Abyssal, might be right. That way, the personal horror for Mage is less &quot;the price of power&quot; and more &quot;holy shit <i>what if <b>I </b>am the monster</i>???&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":10056,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","user":"ShadowKnight1224","date":". 01-26-2016, 10:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T03:36:05-08:00","id":817502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/813286-2ed-lie-dissonance-and-quiescence?p=817336#post817336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I reasoned that the Abyss is probably <i>a very good thing for humanity</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Intruders actually has a section where it speculates on something not unlike that. It doesn't say it's a good thing (it's marginally worse for sleepers in fact), but it suggests that the Abyss could be the reaction of the sleepers to being so horribly dominated by the Awakened. A sort of a spiritual self-mutilation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This viewpoint emphasises an aspect of hubris that I thought wasn't terribly well explored in either edition of mage (though I'd have to read 2e properly to say for sure): the idea that hubris <i>blinds</i>. That mages are convinced that their delusions about reality are true, and that their hubris blinds them to the idea that they might be wrong, </div> </div> </div>It doesn't do that at all. You said the Awakened literally don't see the problem. That's not hubris, that's being unaware of the problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T03:59:13-08:00","id":817506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/813286-2ed-lie-dissonance-and-quiescence?p=817502#post817502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't do that at all. You said the Awakened literally don't see the problem. That's not hubris, that's being unaware of the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are so self-assured that you don't stop to think you might be wrong about the way the world works, particularly when it comes to wielding sorcerous power, I'd call that arrogant at the very least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T04:15:50-08:00","id":817513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/813286-2ed-lie-dissonance-and-quiescence?p=817506#post817506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are so self-assured that you don't stop to think you might be wrong about the way the world works, particularly when it comes to wielding sorcerous power, I'd call that arrogant at the very least.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the way you've changed the setting, even if they do stop and think, they'll find evidence that they're right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T04:52:36-08:00","id":817522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/813286-2ed-lie-dissonance-and-quiescence?p=817513#post817513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the way you've changed the setting, even if they do stop and think, they'll find evidence that they're right.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not precisely what I said. I said that everything in the Mage books was true when perceived by a mage. That means that mages know that their magic harms Sleeper souls. The hubris comes in assuming that it's a flaw in the Sleeper soul rather than in the Supernal Realm. Again, the personal horror in Mage comes from the realisation that hey, maybe you're a soul-shredding warlock rather than an angelic bringer of Supernal Truth. Or hey, maybe you're both, since reality supports both interpretations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T05:19:48-08:00","id":817532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/813286-2ed-lie-dissonance-and-quiescence?p=817522#post817522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That means that mages know that their magic harms Sleeper souls. The hubris comes in assuming that it's a flaw in the Sleeper soul rather than in the Supernal Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, because that's the way it appears to them.<br /> <br /> That's without going into the fact that Mage society already discourages open use of magic. The sleeping curse being a part of the sleepers is explicitly not an excuse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T05:42:18-08:00","id":817539,"title":"","content":"I think this actually helps to explain why it's Wise not to use magic casually, and why it's discouraged to do so unless it's a serious case. It's a tone shift, from &quot;the world is too flawed to handle my magic&quot; to &quot;my magic is too flawed for the world to handle.&quot; You may think that's too subtle a difference, but it genuinely means the world to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T09:02:52-08:00","id":817665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/813286-2ed-lie-dissonance-and-quiescence?p=817336#post817336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Right now, my tentative houserules is to start every single spell with baseline Paradox (so instead of a free Reach, you always risk Paradox no matter how casual the spell is). In 1e, I'd get rid of the Vulgar/Covert system and run all spells as automatically risking Paradox at all times. For Quiescence, I'd run it closer to Lunacy, with the idea that mortals with high Willpower (or that succeed at their Integrity roll) can actually remember what happened, and are likely to become Hunters. I might steal the 2e Lunacy rules and have dramatic failures in the Integrity roll bestow the Proximi minor template.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I also might tweak the Disbelief rules to make sure that mages can't feasibly cast anything that would have any long-term permanent consequences on humanity, like mind-controlling authority figures or any such shenanigans. I'll probably adjust Disbelief so that it can reasonably keep magic in check.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno about the omnipresent Paradox risk. It discourages the subtle approach to magic somewhat. I think making Paradox backlash deal resistant lethal instead of resistant bashing is already a big increase in the danger. I also disagree with giving the Proximi template as a result of an Integrity Breaking Point roll, as Proximi are almost always the result of heritage. I'm fine with giving the Sleepwalker Merit, but my hunch is that a Breaking Point roll isn't the best way to determine when to give it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/813286-2ed-lie-dissonance-and-quiescence?p=817336#post817336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In terms of fluff, my baseline assumption is that mages are completely deluded about the nature of reality. Everything in the Mage books is true, when observed by a Mage. For everyone else, the Supernal Realms are nightmarish hell planes of soul-murder, and the Abyss is the stalwart guardian of humanity against the incursions of the aforementioned planes. Since humanity has a sympathetic connection to the Abyss, I reasoned that the Abyss is probably <i>a very good thing for humanity</i>. I also have Abyssal entities consider regular humans to be kin, to drive this point home. Where Mages see their souls as having &quot;awakened into the truth&quot;, everyone else sees their souls as missing a vital component, which was replaced by a shard of the hellish realms. Paradox, then, is the Abyss trying to protect humanity from the Supernal soul-murder.<br /> <br /> Of course, Exarchs are still the bad guys (because they use the Supernal to actively oppress humanity) and Mad Ones are still terribly dangerous, but even Pentacle mages are hubristic and misguided. Banishers are the closest thing to &quot;heroic mages&quot;, from humanity's perspective, and Scelesti are... complicated.<br /> <br /> This viewpoint emphasises an aspect of hubris that I thought wasn't terribly well explored in either edition of mage (though I'd have to read 2e properly to say for sure): the idea that hubris <i>blinds</i>. That mages are convinced that their delusions about reality are true, and that their hubris blinds them to the idea that they might be wrong, that their actions may not, in fact, be justified. That maybe humanity, in its powerlessness and sympathy for the Abyssal, might be right. That way, the personal horror for Mage is less &quot;the price of power&quot; and more &quot;holy shit <i>what if <b>I </b>am the monster</i>???&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> While I am very fond of giving reality checks to Mages and other supernaturals who never bother to put themselves in another's shoes, defining the Abyss as a guardian of anything is a really big stretch.<br /> <br /> All of that being said, I still like your post.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T06:38:20-08:00","id":828184,"title":"","content":"Interesting question - <b>Chloe Decker, police detective parter of Lucifer - Sleeper or Sleepwalker?</b> She does seem immune to his Mind magic, but also under the Lie? She does not believe him even when he openly say her he is The Devil.,,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XC200bNJ7Q4\" data-code=\"XC200bNJ7Q4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/XC200bNJ7Q4/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T06:56:39-08:00","id":829227,"title":"","content":"Narrative question, typical in magic related fiction - <b>The Sleeper comes to character and says:<i>&quot; I believe in magic. And I know you are mage/</i></b><b><i>witch/</i></b><b><i>wizard.&quot;</i></b><br /> <br /> Question: <b>What now, in Mage setting?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-13-2016, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T07:05:32-08:00","id":829229,"title":"","content":"I personally rule such people as never being able to grasp SUPERNAL magic. Lie revamps their vision of magic into something that maybe calls it magic, but is unable to grasp the true essence of magic, if it makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T07:20:23-08:00","id":829233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/813286-2ed-lie-dissonance-and-quiescence?p=829227#post829227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Narrative question, typical in magic related fiction - <b>The Sleeper comes to character and says:<i>&amp;quot; I believe in magic. And I know you are mage/</i></b><b><i>witch/</i></b><b><i>wizard.&amp;quot;</i></b><br /> <br /> Question: <b>What now, in Mage setting?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>The Mage decides to find a way to make the Sleeper useful or to get rid of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T07:32:53-08:00","id":829238,"title":"","content":"For example, we have typical <i>&quot;crystal gazing hippy&quot;</i>.<b> How would this character react to Supernal Magic cast near him? How he would react to Scrying magic? Time Arcanum prophesies?</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=W3PywlRoAJk\" data-code=\"W3PywlRoAJk\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/W3PywlRoAJk/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/813286-2ed-lie-dissonance-and-quiescence?p=829229#post829229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally rule such people as never being able to grasp SUPERNAL magic. Lie revamps their vision of magic into something that maybe calls it magic, but is unable to grasp the true essence of magic, if it makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Answer to the &quot;crystal gazing hippy&quot; example. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T08:36:21-08:00","id":829262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/813286-2ed-lie-dissonance-and-quiescence?p=829238#post829238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>How would this character react to Supernal Magic cast near him? How he would react to Scrying magic? Time Arcanum prophesies?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>If Supernal magic was cast near them (And by near I'm assuming you mean where they can witness it) then they'd suffer Dissonance. A prophecy is just a side effect of creating a temporal model of the future, and as such won't have any effect on the Sleeper. It's purely Fallen information at that point.<br /> <br /> I don't know why you're raising these questions, anyone can believe in magic. The Sleepers just can't witness it or remember it happening. This has been discussed so many times already, and you've even taken part in these conversations that I'm confused why you can't remember their conclusions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T08:47:54-08:00","id":829266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/813286-2ed-lie-dissonance-and-quiescence?p=829262#post829262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Supernal magic was cast near them (And by near I'm assuming you mean where they can witness it) then they'd suffer Dissonance. A prophecy is just a side effect of creating a temporal model of the future, and as such won't have any effect on the Sleeper. It's purely Fallen information at that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>You see, here is interesting information - <b>Even when there is not destinction of &quot;Cover/Vulgar&quot; spells in 2ED, some magics form <i>are</i> more safe than others for spellcaster. If mage casts divinition spell near Sleeper, but only on themselves - Will it still rise Paradox? Like adding this 9 again trick to Paradox roll?</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/813286-2ed-lie-dissonance-and-quiescence?p=829262#post829262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know why you're raising these questions, anyone can believe in magic. The Sleepers just can't witness it or remember it happening. This has been discussed so many times already, and you've even taken part in these conversations that I'm confused why you can't remember their conclusions.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I pointed above - one thing is academic idea &quot;I understand how this should work&quot;. Totally different is &quot;real world situation&quot;. <b>If I'm right, you can cast almost any Knowing Practice spells on yourself and do not have problems, even when surrounded by people.<br /> <br /> Would then, let's say, possessing by Shadow's spirits one of Sleepers be problem for mage? Would it rise Paradox, Dissonance? IF the only witness is Sleeper going to be possessed?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-13-2016, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T09:06:32-08:00","id":829269,"title":"","content":"Other two examples that come to my head...<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Acanthus Gypsy is reading the future of her Sleeper client by using Time spell with Crystal Ball Yantra or Tarot reading Yantra.</b> Are there Dissonance? Sleeper remembers the reading? Or does he know that his memories on the prophesies itself are &quot;fuzzy&quot; and he cannot recall details?<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Alchemist bartender sells her mixed with Matter and Mind potions using Brewing Yantra.</b> Does Sleepers clients suspects something? Remembers that &quot;those drinks are <i>funny</i> tasting&quot;? They know they are &quot;feeling weird&quot; after them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T09:23:46-08:00","id":829274,"title":"","content":"If the Sleeper has no way of telling that an act of magic has occurred/is occurring then they won't trigger Dissonance or Unravel a spell.<br /> <br /> A Sleeper being possessed by an entity would know that's not right and proceed to Unravel the possession spell.<br /> <br /> If you read the spoilers you'd know this already. It comes up in that scene Dave posted for the Man Comes Around where Cowl is casting curses on that gang leader. He takes notes on what spells aren't obvious, what spells aren't obvious when cast and presumably what spells are obvious when cast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T09:45:42-08:00","id":829287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/813286-2ed-lie-dissonance-and-quiescence?p=829274#post829274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Sleeper has no way of telling that an act of magic has occurred/is occurring then they won't trigger Dissonance or Unravel a spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is - Sleeper comes to the witch and ask for prophecy or potion. He pays hard cash for it. <b>Sleeper is WAITING for the act of magic. He WANT'S it.</b> <b>He ASSUMES that magic is at hand ( if it would be otherwise, he would not come to witch in fist place).</b> Still, Sleeper doesn't &quot;see&quot; the Knowing spell ( witch is ) or do not is participating in potion brewing.<br /> <br /> I <i>assume</i> in prophecy example there is nothing wrong with the spell - it works directly on Acanthus, she has vision, she is free from Quiescence <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">and Dissonance - it's an instant spell </span><i>on her</i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">, not Sleeper. She just later &quot;speak of her mind&quot; to the client.</span><br /> <br /> Interesting thing comes when you analyze potion brewing. <b>Sleeper asked for Potion of Strength. Or Love Potion to make other girl love him. Would it work? </b>Sleeper WANT's magic to work. Sleeper NEEDs it. But there is Dissonance effect and Unraveling that - according to spoilers - have nothing to believes of Sleeper.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/813286-2ed-lie-dissonance-and-quiescence?p=829274#post829274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Sleeper being possessed by an entity would know that's not right and proceed to Unravel the possession spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about willing possession by Loa's in Voodoo? Sleeper <i>wants</i> to be controlled, it's part of his spiritual dogma. Spell just sends Loa instantly, than making complex Manifestations for normal human-spirits interactions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/813286-2ed-lie-dissonance-and-quiescence?p=829274#post829274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It comes up in that scene Dave posted for the Man Comes Around where Cowl is casting curses on that gang leader. He takes notes on what spells aren't obvious, what spells aren't obvious when cast and presumably what spells are obvious when cast.</div> </div> </div> </div>I vaguely remember reading it somewhere, but do not recall where - could you point me to it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-13-2016, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T10:02:14-08:00","id":829295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/813286-2ed-lie-dissonance-and-quiescence?p=829227#post829227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Narrative question, typical in magic related fiction - <b>The Sleeper comes to character and says:<i>&quot; I believe in magic. And I know you are mage/</i></b><b><i>witch/</i></b><b><i>wizard.&quot;</i></b><br /> <br /> Question: <b>What now, in Mage setting?</b></div> </div> </div> </div> It depends on a lot of things, to be perfectly frank. Sleepers now apparently are allowed to be &quot;in the know&quot; about Supernal magic, but still trigger Dissonance. I'm personally still fuzzy on a lot of details on the difference between a Sleeper and Sleepwalker. Not the mechanical difference, the story/background of it. What the line that makes that &quot;abyssal shard&quot; go away. In 1e, I would have said that your Sleeper was either 1) lying to themselves (want to believe, but actually don't), or 2) is actually a budding Sleepwalker. <br /> <br /> In either case, my suggestion would be to put them through the local Msytery Cult and see if they can Awaken on the path. Some of the more secrecy oriented mages (GotV?) might just deny it, and walk away, try to get away, since they don't want someone paying attention for magic and potentially causing Dissonance at a bad time. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, as much as DaveB has been trying to make magic as &quot;objective&quot; as possible, Dissonance is still very much a subjective thing. It still relies on a magically enforced Doubting Thomas effect. They see something magical, the Dissoance kicks in, and suddenly they are dissapointed because the so-called magic is clearly faked, because that's how Dissonance works. Makes you doubt.<br /> <br /> Now, in your crystal ball gazer example? What makes you so sure the fortune teller doesn't have an attainment that lets them fortell the future without risk of Paradox or Dissonance? Personally, I would say that a Sleeper that came in to see a non-Legacy fortune teller, obstinably to see the future, would invoke Dissonance if the reading was too accurate, making any more spellcasting dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T10:39:43-08:00","id":829307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/813286-2ed-lie-dissonance-and-quiescence?p=829287#post829287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is - Sleeper comes to the witch and ask for prophecy or potion. He pays hard cash for it. <b>Sleeper is WAITING for the act of magic. He WANT'S it.</b> <b>He ASSUMES that magic is at hand ( if it would be otherwise, he would not come to witch in fist place).</b> Still, Sleeper doesn't &quot;see&quot; the Knowing spell ( witch is ) or do not is participating in potion brewing.<br /> <br /> I <i>assume</i> in prophecy example there is nothing wrong with the spell - it works directly on Acanthus, she has vision, she is free from Quiescence <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">and Dissonance - it's an instant spell </span><i>on her</i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">, not Sleeper. She just later &quot;speak of her mind&quot; to the client.</span><br /> <br /> Interesting thing comes when you analyze potion brewing. <b>Sleeper asked for Potion of Strength. Or Love Potion to make other girl love him. Would it work? </b>Sleeper WANT's magic to work. Sleeper NEEDs it. But there is Dissonance effect and Unraveling that - according to spoilers - have nothing to believes of Sleeper.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What about willing possession by Loa's in Voodoo? Sleeper <i>wants</i> to be controlled, it's part of his spiritual dogma. Spell just sends Loa instantly, than making complex Manifestations for normal human-spirits interactions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I vaguely remember reading it somewhere, but do not recall where - could you point me to it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seems pretty obvious to me, they'd get the potion or the possession or whatever with a warning, it's bad for them and they won't remember what they did during the time spent under its influence. As soon as they experience the effects of the spell kicking in Unraveling will begin and at the end of the scene if the spell has been Unraveled or ended its Duration or whatever then Dissonance will kick in. It doesn't matter what the Sleeper wants, or believes, they'll still suffer. Though on the bright side, they might get what they wanted so badly they'd do that to themselves before the spell is Unraveled and Dissonance kicks in. So even if they can't remember what they did, they can remember that they did something and it involved that Mage and they might even feel like it was worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T10:46:50-07:00","id":974523,"title":"","content":"Next great comic book example on Quiescence - this time from <b>Lock &amp; Key</b> series. And related question - <b>Do children in Mage less likely to get </b><b>Quiescence </b><b>from magic?</b><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/3soLo7r.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/dAwjydK.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"